      "writtenOn": "2026-09-03T15:42:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s always fatal in EL2, as the hypervisor doesn\u0027t handle BRK, it will panic. This kind of error handling is commonly used (as in mem_protect.c) to avoid complex error handling in situations that shouldn\u0027t happen.\n\nIn this specific situation, I think it\u0027s safe to `return ret` and leak the reference. But if the HW is timing out, the system probably won\u0027t survive for longer.\nI can to update the code to be tolerant.",
